ready: 1
kind: system
id: sys.home
name: Kernle home
role: Holds every Kernle file for one OS account, with one directory and database per stack
system_kind: storage
hosting: The owner's disk, under the home directory
code: ~/.kernle
responsibilities:
  - The stack registry, configuration, daemon socket, and downloaded model
  - One database and export folder per stack
secrets:
  - KERNLE_CREDENTIALS_FALLBACK
notes: >-
  Layout: `registry.db`, `config.toml`, `run/kernled.sock`, `models/`,
  `stacks/<stack_id>/kernle.db`, and `stacks/<stack_id>/export/`. The
  credentials fallback file exists only on Linux hosts without a keychain.
